Linked list are stored in non contiguous manner.

Insertion is really easy in the linked list but, to get any element the Time Complexity is O(n).

Types of Linked List:-
    1.Singly Linked List: Each node is connected to the next node.
    2.Doubly Linked List: Each node is connected to the next and the previous node.
    3.Circular Linked List: All the connection of nodes forms a circle.

Every node in the Linked list consist of tow data types:-
    1. Stores the data like integer values.
    2. Stores the address of the next node.(Last node contains null instead of address).

First node is called head and the last node is called tail.